#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:332
msgid "set_env and unset_env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:334
msgid "See `env`_ tag description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:337
msgid "push_ros_namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:339
msgid ""
"``include`` and ``group`` tags don't accept an ``ns`` attribute. This action "
"can be used as a workaround:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:342
msgid ""
"<!-Other tags-->\n"
"<group>\n"
"   <push_ros_namespace namespace=\"my_ns\"/>\n"
"   <!--Nodes here are namespaced with \"my_ns\".-->\n"
"   <!--If there is an include action here, its nodes will also be "
"namespaced.-->\n"
"   <push_ros_namespace namespace=\"another_ns\"/>\n"
"   <!--Nodes here are namespaced with \"another_ns/my_ns\".-->\n"
"   <push_ros_namespace namespace=\"/absolute_ns\"/>\n"
"   <!--Nodes here are namespaced with \"/absolute_ns\".-->\n"
"   <!--The following node receives an absolute namespace, so it will ignore "
"the others previously pushed.-->\n"
"   <!--The full path of the node will be /asd/my_node.-->\n"
"   <node pkg=\"my_pkg\" exec=\"my_executable\" name=\"my_node\" namespace=\"/"
"asd\"/>\n"
"</group>\n"
"<!--Nodes outside the group action won't be namespaced.-->\n"
"<!-Other tags-->"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:361
msgid "let"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:363
msgid "It's a replacement of ``arg`` tag with a value attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:365
msgid "<let name=\"foo\" value=\"asd\"/>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:369
msgid "``let`` and ``arg`` serve two different purposes in ROS 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:371
msgid "``let`` sets a launch configuration value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:372
msgid ""
"``arg`` declares a launch argument/configuration and optionally provides a "
"default value. The value can separately be set from the CLI or when "
"including the given launch file. If no value is set, the default value is "
"used if one was provided, otherwise an error is reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:377
msgid "executable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:379
msgid "It allows running any executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:384
msgid ""
"<executable cmd=\"ls -las\" cwd=\"/var/log\" name=\"my_exec\" launch-"
"prefix=\"something\" output=\"screen\" shell=\"true\">\n"
"   <env name=\"LD_LIBRARY\" value=\"/lib/some.so\"/>\n"
"</executable>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:391
msgid "Replacing an include tag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:393
msgid ""
"In order to include a launch file under a **namespace** as in ROS 1 then the "
"``include`` tags must be nested in a ``group`` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:395
msgid ""
"<group>\n"
"   <include file=\"another_launch_file\"/>\n"
"</group>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:401
msgid ""
"Then, instead of using the ``ns`` attribute, add the ``push_ros_namespace`` "
"action tag to specify the namespace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:403
msgid ""
"<group>\n"
"   <push_ros_namespace namespace=\"my_ns\"/>\n"
"   <include file=\"another_launch_file\"/>\n"
"</group>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:410
msgid ""
"Nesting ``include`` tags under a ``group`` tag is only required when "
"specifying a namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:413
msgid "Substitutions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:415
msgid ""
"Documentation about ROS 1's substitutions can be found in `roslaunch XML "
"wiki <https://wiki.ros.org/roslaunch/XML>`__. Substitutions syntax hasn't "
"changed, i.e. it still follows the ``$(substitution-name arg1 arg2 ...)`` "
"pattern. There are, however, some changes w.r.t. ROS 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:419
msgid ""
"``env`` and ``optenv`` tags have been replaced by the ``env`` tag. ``$(env "
"<NAME>)`` will fail if the environment variable doesn't exist. ``$(env "
"<NAME> '')`` does the same as ROS 1's ``$(optenv <NAME>)``. ``$(env <NAME> "
"<DEFAULT>)`` does the same as ROS 1's ``$(env <NAME> <DEFAULT>)`` or "
"``$(optenv <NAME> <DEFAULT>)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:423
msgid ""
"``find`` has been replaced with ``find-pkg-share`` (substituting the share "
"directory of an installed package). Alternatively ``find-pkg-prefix`` will "
"return the root of an installed package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:425
msgid ""
"There is a new ``exec-in-pkg`` substitution. e.g.: ``$(exec-in-pkg "
"<exec_name> <package_name>)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:427
msgid "There is a new ``find-exec`` substitution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:428
msgid ""
"``arg`` has been replaced with ``var``. It looks at configurations defined "
"either with ``arg`` or ``let`` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:430
msgid ""
"``eval`` and ``dirname`` substitutions require escape characters for string "
"values, e.g. ``if=\"$(eval '\\'$(var variable)\\' == \\'val1\\'')\"``. You "
"can also use HTML escapes like ``&quot;`` ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:432
msgid ""
"Boolean predicates can also be expressed directly with the ``equals``, ``not-"
"equals``, ``and``, ``or``, ``any``, and ``all`` substitutions. For example, "
"``if=\"$(equals $(var variable) val1)\"`` is equivalent to ``if=\"$(eval "
"'\\'$(var variable)\\' == \\'val1\\'')\"``. See :ref:`Boolean substitutions "
"<BooleanSubstitutions>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:435
msgid ""
"``eval`` does not pass configurations ( ``arg`` ) as local Python variables. "
"They have to be accessed via ``$(var name)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:437
msgid ""
"The argument of ``eval`` has to be a quoted string in ROS 2. That is also "
"the reason why quotes inside the expression have to be escaped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:443
msgid ""
"The rules that were shown in ``Type inference rules`` subsection of "
"``param`` tag applies to any attribute. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:446
msgid ""
"<!--Setting a string value to an attribute expecting an int will raise an "
"error.-->\n"
"<tag1 attr-expecting-an-int=\"'1'\"/>\n"
"<!--Correct version.-->\n"
"<tag1 attr-expecting-an-int=\"1\"/>\n"
"<!--Setting an integer in an attribute expecting a string will raise an "
"error.-->\n"
"<tag2 attr-expecting-a-str=\"1\"/>\n"
"<!--Correct version.-->\n"
"<tag2 attr-expecting-a-str=\"'1'\"/>\n"
"<!--Setting a list of strings in an attribute expecting a string will raise "
"an error.-->\n"
"<tag3 attr-expecting-a-str=\"asd, bsd\" str-attr-sep=\", \"/>\n"
"<!--Correct version.-->\n"
"<tag3 attr-expecting-a-str=\"don't use a separator\"/>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files.rst:461
msgid ""
"Some attributes accept more than a single type, for example ``value`` "
"attribute of ``param`` tag. It's usual that parameters that are of type "
"``int`` (or ``float``) also accept an ``str``, that will be later "
"substituted and tried to convert to an ``int`` (or ``float``) by the action."
msgstr ""
